item.description:
arXiv:2605.12300v2 Announce Type: replace 
Abstract: We prove a range of rigidity results for quasiisometric embeddings between right-angled Artin groups. Among other things, we:
  (1) classify all self--quasiisometric-embeddings of RAAGs defined on cycles;
  (2) show that no $n$--dimensional RAAG is a universal receiver for quasiisometric embeddings of $n$--dimensional RAAGs.
  (3) prove that if the direct product $F_2^n\times A_{C_5}^m$ can be quasiisometrically embedded in a RAAG $A_\Gamma$ of the same dimension, then the defining graph of $F_2^n\times A_{C_5}^m$ must appear as an induced subgraph of $\Gamma$;
  We also establish a strong rigidity theorem for quasiisometrically embedded images of 2--flats in RAAGs defined by triangle-free graphs that are not stars, generalising a theorem of Bestvina--Kleiner--Sageev.
